Patch files in this image (/opt/aeon/patches/inkling2)
-----------------------------------------------------
0001-0006: the cleanroom series from ~/inkling/engines/aeon-cleanroom/patches/inkling2.
  Verified: they apply in order, cleanly, onto 1fd30e4f6. They are already in this
  tree as the six commits above. Later commits edited the same files, so the
  original patch files do not reverse-apply onto HEAD.

0007-0018: git format-patch of c1e83ffed..HEAD (merge a76700f7f omitted, as
  format-patch skips merges). End state is 0714f860c.

Note on numbering vs https://github.com/AEON-7/vllm-ultimate-rocm PRs #2-#6:
  Those PRs numbered the ablation patch as 0013 (after the M2 kernel patches)
  because they reordered it for the stacked patch series. This image's 0009 is
  the same ablation commit 70e97ec3c, and 0018 is the new R6 patch (not yet
  in those PRs). Feature set at HEAD is the union of PRs #2-#6 plus R6.

Features included
-----------------
- Inkling 2 Small + Inkling-2-Mini (inkling2_loop) on gfx1201 (R9700)
- NVFP4 / MXFP8 routed experts, loop ops, per-pass KV and conv state
- AEON research hooks: weight overlay, activation capture, runtime o_proj ablation
- M2 gfx12 decode kernels (MoE, GEMV, fused blend/router/sconv, K/V taps)
- Multi-variant per-request o_proj ablation
- Mixed-batch determinism: batch-invariant MoE mode (c1d310e97, VLLM_BATCH_INVARIANT)
  There is no separately named "exact mode" commit; this is that work.
- DSpark (opt-in at serve time via speculative-config; AEON_DSPARK_GEMV defaults to 1)
- R5 per-request residual-stream variant edits
- R6 r5_bake --readers all, plus CPU and GPU bake-vs-hook tools
- tools/inkling2: r5_bake.py, test_r5_bake.py, test_r6_bake.py, r6_validate.py, r6_run.sh
- /opt/aeon/scripts: cleanroom aeon/ validation and unit scripts (57 files)
- env.sh flags baked as image ENV (see stack pins). No expandable_segments.

